      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address the \"unlevel playing field,\" argue that these local regulations create a significant competitive disadvantage, forcing your plant to absorb high compliance costs that your unregulated international competitors avoid, effectively making it more expensive to do the same good in the US. The primary argument the representatives will likely use for the necessity of the rules is the public good and the \"external cost\" of pollution, emphasizing the imperative to protect local air and public health from climate change.",
      "source": "target",
