      "content": "From a strictly pragmatic viewpoint, you can argue that the regulations prioritize ideological compliance over a true, comprehensive cost-benefit analysis for the local economy. You can advocate for a \"phased and supportive\" approach, suggesting that the *process of implementation* is the real flaw, not the end goal of cleaner air, to make the policy politically and economically viable for the community. This reframing shifts the debate from \"should we comply\" to \"how can we comply support",
      "source": "target",
